# This is the processing directive for bi-temporal Anchor Modeling in Vertica
#
# The templates are in the Sisula language (docs/SISULA.md) and render the JSON bindings that the
# modeler builds (Generate > JSON bindings). The scripts first in the list prepare the schema that the
# bindings are made from; they run once, before the templates. A line starting with # is not run.
#
# Vertica has no function that returns a table, so the rewinders are views of what is known now, and of the perspectives
# only the latest and the now perspectives are made. It has no triggers either.
SQL/Helpers.js
SQL/NamingConvention.js
SQL/Vertica/NamingConvention.js
SQL/Vertica/derive.js
SQL/Vertica/CreateSchemas.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateKnots.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateAnchors.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateNexuses.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateAttributes.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateAttributeAssembledViews.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateAttributeRewinders.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateAnchorPerspectives.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateNexusPerspectives.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateTies.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateTieAssembledViews.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateTieRewinders.sisula
SQL/Vertica/bi/CreateTiePerspectives.sisula
SQL/Vertica/AddDescriptions.sisula
